Z||000000||sparks||08-15-2001||10:21 PM||||Background info on car: 1985 4 cylinder, Fiero Store "Vented Front Brake Upgrade Kit" just put on a month ago.  When I took the car in to the shop for an alignement it was fine, got it aligned and now the steering wheel vibrates above 60 mph.<P>Any ideas?  I haven't taken it apart to look at it yet, I just found this out tonite and it just got dark.  I plan to dissasemble the front tomorrow nite and have a look at it.  <P>Also it seems that two of my front studs are no longer secure in the hub, I can't tighten them down now either.  Could before the shop aligned it...<P>Arrghhh!  I haven't had the car to drive in a month now due to the e-brake hanging up, which is now fixed.  But now it does this!<P>I'm about ready to put stock back on and see what I can get, if anything out of the kit and see if that fixes it.  If not I still feel like it's a step ahead from what I've read about the kits now and with my lugs not being secure in the hub anymore.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||13
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-15-2001||10:27 PM||||did they change any of the tires to a diff position. some put the best tires on the front to align it. Depending on what equipment they use, they may have taken wheel weights off to attach it and didnt get them on in same position. Just sounds like Out of balance to me, nothing to do with actual alignment. The loose studs could be because they changed your wheels around with a cranked up air gun. I always make sure they do mine by hand, I watch them. Old story, My Mercedes AMG had special wheels and a tire guy used an impact on them and messed them up, made them buy me 4 new wheels for $2000.00<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||08-16-2001||07:48 AM||||Sounds like a wheel balance problem.  Unless the alignment shop screwed up the stud or put the 215/60's on the front the 205/60's on the back or mixed them all up.<P>Mine had a wobble, it was just the wheel balance was off.  I hope it is that simple.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sparks||08-16-2001||08:59 AM||||Yes, I'm hoping it's as simple as a tire out of balance.  However I'm not sure the lugs will be that simple.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>There's one on either side.  Unfortunately I had to get back to work and couldn't stay and watch them when they put everything back together.  Oh and front and rear tires are the same size, so if the rears were out of balance and they switched 'em it's possible I suppose.<P>I'm going to give them a call today and see what they have to say about it.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
